    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Salineño, TX is a quaint, 250‑year‑old community, once the headquarters of Rancho Salinas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/salineno-tx",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ranching in the Salineño area began in 1734, and by 1757 five ranches owned 4,000 horses, cattle and 40,000 sheep and goats.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/salineno-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1900 a single Spanish‑speaking teacher ran a wooden school for nineteen pupils, later replaced by a brick building in 1937.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/salineno-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A rural water system serving Falcon Heights and Falcon Village replaced the old water wagon that filled the town's cisterns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/salineno-tx",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In 1990 Salineño had three stores, a church, a post office, a waterworks, a well‑kept cemetery, and 155 inhabitants.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
